00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:46.220
Season 2, Episode 6, written by Gene Stupnitsky and Lee Eisenberg, known to us as Gene and Lee.
第二季第六集，由吉恩·斯图普尼茨基和李·艾森伯格编剧，我们称他们为吉恩和李。

201
00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:46.860
They're a duo.
他们是一对搭档。

202
00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:47.980
They're funny fellas.
他们是很有趣的家伙。

203
00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.480
This episode was directed by Ken Kwapis.
这一集是由肯·夸皮斯执导的。

204
00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.160
We love Ken Kwapis.
我们爱肯·夸皮斯。

205
00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.020
We love Ken Kwapis.
我们爱肯·夸皮斯。

206
00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:59.420
I don't even know if it's possible for people to understand our love of Ken Kwapis.
我甚至不知道人们是否能理解我们对肯·夸皮斯的喜爱。

207
00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:00.540
I don't know, guys.
我不知道，伙计们。

208
00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.920
There are some directors that just are in our hearts.
有些导演就是走进了我们的心里。

209
00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:07.000
Ken Kwapis, Paul Feig, Charles McDougal.
肯·夸皮斯、保罗·费格、查尔斯·麦克道格。

210
00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:07.920
Charles McDougal.
查尔斯·麦克道格。

211
00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.180
For yelling action at us.
因为他们对我们喊过“开始”。

212
00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:09.840
For a different way, though.
不过是以不同的方式。

213
00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:12.320
Like, Ken Kwapis is like a cozy blanket.
比如，肯·夸皮斯就像一条舒适的毯子。

214
00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.440
Paul Feig, you want to hang out with all day.
保罗·费格，你会想和他待上一整天。

215
00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:15.420
And drink martinis.
喝喝马提尼。

216
00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:21.020
Charles McDougal, you kind of want to get drunk in a pub with and yell at people.
查尔斯·麦克道格，你会想和他一起在酒吧喝醉，然后对着别人大喊大叫。

217
00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:23.360
It's so true.
太对了。

218
00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.660
We'll talk about Charles McDougal when we get to him.
等我们聊到查尔斯·麦克道格时再细说。

219
00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.400
We haven't really had a chance to talk about him, but that was a little preview.
我们还没机会好好聊聊他，但刚才算是小小的预告。

220
00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:30.900
We have a special treat today.
今天我们有个特别节目。

221
00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:35.740
Our summary of this episode is going to be read by a fan.
我们这一集的剧情梗概将由一位粉丝来朗读。

222
00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:36.600
Dun, dun, dun.
当当当。

223
00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:37.760
So here we go.
那么，我们开始吧。

224
00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.260
Alexis is describing the fight.
亚历克西斯正在描述这场打斗。

225
00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.820
Dwight becomes assistant to the sensei at his dojo and spends the day bragging and telling everyone how tough he is.
德怀特成了他道场教练的助手，整天吹嘘并告诉每个人他有多强悍。

226
00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.880
Michael has a lot of papers to sign.
迈克尔有很多文件要签。

227
00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:52.580
Jim and Pam use the opportunity to trick Michael by saying they think Dwight is stronger than Michael is.
吉姆和帕姆趁机捉弄迈克尔，说他们觉得德怀特比迈克尔更强。

228
00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:57.080
So Michael agrees to duel Dwight at the dojo to prove his manliness and procrastinate doing his work.
于是迈克尔同意在道场和德怀特决斗，以证明自己的男子气概，同时也为了拖延工作。

229
00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.480
I thought that was very good.
我觉得写得非常好。

230
00:07:58.600 --> 00:07:59.220
That was really good.
真的写得很好。

231
00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:00.180
I feel like she covered it.
我觉得她概括得很到位。

232
00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:01.500
She was very concise.
她非常简洁。

233
00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.540
I feel like maybe she wrote it down and read it, which is what I would do.
我觉得她可能是写下来读的，如果是我也会这么做。

234
00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:05.480
So, Alexis.
那么，亚历克西斯。

235
00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.500
Alexis, you've made a friend.
亚历克西斯，你交到朋友了。

236
00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.160
That's right.
没错。

237
00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:11.260
All right.
好的。

238
00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.840
Let's get into the fast facts for the fight.
让我们进入关于“打斗”这一集的速览环节。

239
00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:15.860
Fast fact number one.
速览第一点。

240
00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:20.360
This is the first episode from our new writing team of Jean and Lee.
这是我们新的编剧团队吉恩和李创作的第一集。

241
00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:32.540
I emailed with Lee Eisenberg, and he told me that before getting hired on the office, Jean was a part-time nanny, and Lee was an assistant to a director.
我和李·艾森伯格通过邮件交流过，他告诉我，在被《办公室》聘用之前，吉恩是一名兼职保姆，而李是一位导演的助理。

242
00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:36.020
This was their first staff writing job.
这是他们第一份正式的编剧工作。

243
00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:40.360
They were over the moon, and they were particularly excited about the free lunches.
他们当时欣喜若狂，尤其是对免费午餐感到特别兴奋。

244
00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.580
I can really relate to that.
我真的很有同感。

245
00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:44.460
I can, too.
我也是。

246
00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.600
When I interned on Conan O'Brien, I got free food, and I was so excited.
我在柯南·奥布莱恩节目组实习时，能吃到免费食物，我当时兴奋极了。

247
00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:56.820
Every time I got a job as an actor, when I was a struggling actor, I got excited about the free meals, the free food at work.
当我还是个挣扎求生的演员时，每次接到工作，我都会为工作餐的免费食物感到兴奋。

248
00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:57.640
It's a big deal.
这可是件大事。

249
00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:00.240
I kind of still get excited about it, I have to be honeSt.
老实说，我现在还是会为此感到兴奋。

250
00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:01.280
The snack tables.
零食台。

251
00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.480
I hate to break it to everyone at Earwolf, but I hit up that fruit bowl hard every morning when we come here.
我不想扫大家的兴，但每次我们来Earwolf，我早上都会把那个水果碗扫荡一空。

252
00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:06.900
Yeah.
没错。

253
00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:08.040
Like apple, banana.
比如苹果、香蕉之类的。

254
00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.160
Earwolf has a basket of chips that's really good, too.
Earwolf还有一篮薯片，也特别好吃。

255
00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:21.680
When I worked in offices in real life, I used to get really excited to go in the break room, and someone would bring in some Danish or some muffins or cookies.
我以前在现实中的办公室工作时，去休息室总是特别兴奋，因为总有人会带些丹麦酥、松饼或饼干过来。

256
00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:22.660
I don't know.
我不知道。

257
00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:27.100
If you were anything like me, I would eat ramen noodles because you could buy nine for a dollar.
如果你像我一样，我以前常吃方便面，因为一块钱能买九包。

258
00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:28.160
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

259
00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:28.760
Oh, man.
天呐。

260
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:33.560
You know, ramen noodles are really a great meal for family meals with kids.
你知道吗，方便面其实很适合做家庭餐，尤其是给孩子吃。

261
00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.960
You can spruce it up.
你可以稍微加工一下。

262
00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:39.900
You can sauté some brown chicken and put a bunch of veggies in with the noodles.
你可以炒点鸡肉丁，再往面里加一大堆蔬菜。

263
00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:47.060
You can also not cook them at all and crunch them up and put them in a salad instead of a crouton.
你也可以干脆不煮，直接捏碎了撒在沙拉里当面包丁用。

264
00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.320
This has turned into a different show.
这节目画风突变啊。

265
00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:49.880
Okay.
好吧。

266
00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.780
That's like a – you can make a Chinese chicken salad.
这就好比——你可以做个中式鸡肉沙拉。

267
00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.700
You can use ramen noodles as your crunchies.
你可以用方便面来增加脆脆的口感。

268
00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:55.260
Wow.
哇。

269
00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:56.120
There you go.
就是这样。

270
00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:59.620
Some more information from Lee about this being his first episode.
关于这是Lee的第一集，还有些补充信息。

271
00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:08.080
He said they were terrified because remember we talked about how they break down the episodes as a group and then writers get assigned to write the episode?
他说他们当时吓坏了，还记得我们聊过他们是怎么分组拆解剧集，然后分配编剧去写剧本的吗？

272
00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:17.040
He said that since their episode was episode six, they had very little in their outline.
他说因为他们负责的是第六集，大纲里的内容非常少。

273
00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:24.700
He said they had fleshed out the other episodes much more than this one, and he thought that they were being set up to fail.
他说其他集的大纲都比这一集充实得多，他觉得他们是被故意设局要让他们失败。

274
00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.060
They were being tested.
他们是在接受考验。

275
00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:33.240
Yes, exactly, because he was like, how do you give the staff writers with the least amount of experience the least worked on outline?
没错，确实如此，因为他当时就在想，怎么能把最没经验的编剧团队分配到大纲最简陋的那一集呢？

276
00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.220
Yes, exactly.
没错，确实。

277
00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:43.360
He said after they turned in their script and they had to get their notes on their script, Greg had pneumonia, and they had to go to Greg's house in order to get their notes.
他说在他们交了剧本等着拿修改意见时，Greg得了肺炎，他们不得不去Greg家里拿意见。

278
00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:52.280
And he said the thing that really stood out to him was that he explained the idea of the Jim-Pam subtext to Gene and Lee.
他说让他印象最深的是，Greg向Gene和Lee解释了Jim和Pam之间潜台词的概念。

279
00:10:52.460 --> 00:11:00.780
They had written a really on-the-nose Jim-Pam scene, and Greg said, sometimes just a look is enough.
他们当时写了一场非常直白的Jim和Pam的戏，Greg说，有时候一个眼神就足够了。

280
00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:07.500
And he said it kind of blew their minds and that Greg completely brought that idea to them.
他说这让他们大开眼界，是Greg把这个想法完全传达给了他们。

281
00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:15.200
And in the episode, something I remember is when Pam is reading Jim's palm, that was a big deal.
在这一集里，我记得有一幕是Pam给Jim看手相，那可是件大事。

282
00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:24.000
It was how – there was always this discussion, how can Jim and Pam physically touch without it being inappropriate?
当时一直在讨论，Jim和Pam怎样才能在不显得不妥的情况下产生肢体接触？

283
00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:24.640
Right.
对。

284
00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:27.780
Well, lady, I think that was very intimate.
哎呀，我觉得那场戏非常亲密。

285
00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:32.460
I even looked up online about hand-touching, and it is considered physical intimacy.
我甚至在网上查过关于手部接触的资料，那确实被视为一种身体上的亲密行为。

286
00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.280
That was some major flirting.
那可是相当明显的调情。

287
00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:35.940
That's a note card I have for later.
那是我留着待会儿要说的卡片内容。

288
00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:36.400
All right.
好吧。

289
00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.600
Should we move on to fast fact number two?
我们要进入第二个速览事实了吗？

290
00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:39.320
Let's do it.
开始吧。

291
00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:39.700
All right.
好的。

292
00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:44.460
Fast fact number two, Sensei Ira was played by Lance Kroll.
第二个速览事实，Ira老师是由Lance Kroll饰演的。

293
00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.880
Is it Sensei or Sensei?
是念Sensei还是Sensei？

294
00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:50.860
Oh, my gosh.
天呐。

295
00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:54.520
It's Sensei Ira was played by Lance Kroll, who's a friend of mine.
是Ira老师，由Lance Kroll饰演，他是我朋友。

296
00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:58.980
And I have five note cards on him because he and I talked on the phone yesterday.
关于他我准备了五张卡片，因为我们昨天刚通过电话。

297
00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:03.940
Oh, you know that I was very starstruck by him when he was on our episode.
噢，你知道的，他上我们那一集的时候，我简直被他迷住了。

298
00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:04.640
I know.
我知道。

299
00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.040
He even said, I think Jenna watched a lot of Joe Schmo.
他甚至说，我觉得Jenna看了很多《乔·施莫大行动》。

300
00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:08.720
Yes.
是的。

301
00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:14.080
That cracks me up that he said that because I did corner him at lunch one day, and I made
他说了那番话让我笑得不行，因为有天午饭时我确实把他堵住了，还逼着

302
00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.120
him tell me everything about the Joe Schmo show.
他把《乔·施莫秀》的一切都告诉了我。

303
00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:18.920
If you guys have not seen this, please go look it up.
如果你们还没看过这个节目，请一定要去搜来看看。

304
00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:28.160
The Joe Schmo show was a fake reality show contest where everybody on the show were actors
《乔·施莫秀》是一档虚构的真人秀比赛，节目里除了一个人之外，

305
00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:29.940
except for one person.
所有人都是演员。

306
00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:31.480
The Joe Schmo guy.
那个“乔·施莫”本人。

307
00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:31.940
Yes.
没错。

308
00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.300
Was a real person.
是个真实的人。

309
00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:37.040
And everyone around him was acting like they were in a reality show.
而他周围的所有人都假装在参加真人秀。

310
00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:37.480
Yes.
是的。

311
00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:42.760
And they were locked in this house, and they had to do competitions and vote each other
他们被关在一栋房子里，必须参加各种比赛，最后还要互相投票

312
00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:43.700
off at the end.
淘汰对方。

313
00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:47.560
By the way, Kristen Wiig is on that show with Lance.
顺便说一下，克里斯汀·韦格和兰斯一起参加了那个节目。

314
00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:51.480
A lot of great comedians and improvisers that I knew were on that show.
我认识的很多优秀的喜剧演员和即兴表演者都参加过那个节目。

315
00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:52.760
I auditioned for that.
我当时也去试镜了。

316
00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:59.140
It was cast by Alison Jones, and I was devastated when I did not get it because I thought, what
那是艾莉森·琼斯选角的，没选上我特别难过，因为我觉得，能住进一栋房子里全天候扮演一个角色，

317
00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:05.380
an amazing acting experience to live in a house and have to play this character 24-7.
那该是多么棒的表演体验啊。

318
00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:07.460
And by the way, the show is brilliant.
顺便提一句，这节目真的太天才了。

319
00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.800
So yes, I am starstruck by Lance.
所以没错，我对兰斯简直是迷弟/迷妹心态。

320
00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:10.980
I can't believe you know him.
真不敢相信你认识他。

321
00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.640
I can't believe I didn't know that you know him.
