00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:29.640
in our garage.
在我们的车库里。

469
00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:30.040
Yeah.
没错。

470
00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:32.340
So this won't be the last time you see Sensei Ira.
所以这不会是你最后一次见到艾拉老师。

471
00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:36.120
He does come back in season nine in the episode Junior Salesman.
他在第九季的《初级推销员》那一集中确实回来了。

472
00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:37.320
He does?
真的吗？

473
00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:38.000
Yes.
是的。

474
00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:39.200
What does he do in that episode?
他在那一集里做了什么？

475
00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:41.800
He was actually there to interview for a job.
他其实是去面试工作的。

476
00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:42.880
Oh, I remember that.
哦，我想起来了。

477
00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:48.840
Oh, Dwight brings in a bunch of his old friends and weirdos to interview.
哦，德怀特带了一群老朋友和怪人来面试。

478
00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:49.960
And, like, family members.
还有一些家庭成员。

479
00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:50.440
Yes.
没错。

480
00:19:50.740 --> 00:19:55.500
Lance emailed me a great behind-the-scenes photo of him and the other people interviewing
兰斯给我发了一张很棒的幕后照片，是他和其他人在会议室里

481
00:19:55.500 --> 00:20:03.400
for jobs in the conference room, and he has his karate outfit on over a business suit.
面试时的合影，他穿着西装，外面还套着空手道服。

482
00:20:03.540 --> 00:20:04.980
So his tie is, like, poking out.
所以他的领带就那么露在外面。

483
00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.160
It's, like, so odd.
看起来太奇怪了。

484
00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:09.500
But, yeah, he was on season one and then on season nine.
不过，没错，他第一季和第九季都出现了。

485
00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:13.440
So he sort of had this great perspective of being on the bookends of the show.
所以他算是从头到尾见证了这部剧，视角很独特。

486
00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.340
What a very, very cool thing.
这真是太酷了。

487
00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:15.740
Yeah.
是啊。

488
00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:20.560
Thank you so much, Lance, for taking time out of your schedule in Atlanta to chat me up.
非常感谢兰斯，在亚特兰大百忙之中抽空和我聊天。

489
00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:23.060
And we're going to call you again come Junior Salesman.
等到《初级推销员》那一集时，我们还会再找你。

490
00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:23.520
Yeah.
好的。

491
00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:24.280
I love it.
我很期待。

492
00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:24.820
All right.
好的。

493
00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:27.740
Let's take a break, and we'll be back to break down the fight.
我们先休息一下，回来后继续拆解这场打斗戏。

494
00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:37.020
We are back.
我们回来了。

495
00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:37.560
Hello.
大家好。

496
00:20:38.220 --> 00:20:40.820
This episode begins with a prank.
这一集以一个恶作剧开场。

497
00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:44.540
Jim pranks Dwight by putting his desk in the bathroom.
吉姆把德怀特的办公桌搬进了洗手间，以此捉弄他。

498
00:20:45.220 --> 00:20:46.260
Oh, poor Dwight.
哦，可怜的德怀特。

499
00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.160
This was a good one.
这个恶作剧很棒。

500
00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:48.300
This was a good prank.
这真是一个精彩的恶作剧。

501
00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:49.360
I like this one.
我喜欢这一幕。

502
00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:53.140
You have to look for Kevin in the background at the end when he leaves one of the stalls.
在最后凯文从隔间出来的时候，你们得留意一下背景里的他。

503
00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.440
He has a lit candle and a newspaper.
他手里拿着一支点燃的蜡烛和一份报纸。

504
00:20:55.800 --> 00:21:01.200
And for all of you office geeks, this was the moment that led to Kevin's line in Office
对于所有《办公室》的铁粉来说，正是这一刻引出了凯文在“办公室奥运会”里说的那句台词，

505
00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:04.580
Olympics about the bathroom candle smelling like cookies.
关于厕所里的蜡烛闻起来像曲奇饼干。

506
00:21:05.520 --> 00:21:11.260
Also, remember that in the Dundies, he did win the Don't Go In There After Me award.
另外，别忘了在“邓迪奖”颁奖礼上，他确实赢得了“别在我之后进去”奖。

507
00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:11.840
Yes.
没错。

508
00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.360
And I think we see why.
我想我们现在明白原因了。

509
00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:18.320
Also, though, guys, who is lighting candles inside the stall?
不过话说回来，伙计们，谁会在隔间里点蜡烛啊？

510
00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:21.940
Like, he doesn't come out and light the candle.
他不是出来之后才点的蜡烛。

511
00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:26.020
He exits the stall holding a candle, a lit candle.
他走出隔间时就拿着一支蜡烛，一支点燃的蜡烛。

512
00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:26.660
Yes.
是的。

513
00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.500
And that candle really did smell like cookies.
而且那支蜡烛闻起来确实像曲奇饼干。

514
00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:29.440
I want to say that.
我想提一下这个。

515
00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:34.860
Did you notice that there is another door by the urinal, Angela?
安吉拉，你注意到小便池旁边还有另一扇门了吗？

516
00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:35.760
Where does it go?
那扇门通向哪里？

517
00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:36.640
We don't know.
我们不知道。

518
00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:37.960
I like to think maybe—
我倾向于认为也许——

519
00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:38.700
What is that door?
那扇门是什么？

520
00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:40.100
Is it a utility closet?
是杂物间吗？

521
00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:40.840
That's what I think.
我也是这么想的。

522
00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:43.260
I think there's like a mop in there or something.
我觉得里面可能放着拖把之类的东西。

523
00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:44.200
That's my guess.
我猜是这样。

524
00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:44.780
Yeah.
没错。

525
00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.620
Those bathrooms did not work.
那些厕所根本不能用。

526
00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:47.020
Nope.
没错。

527
00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.100
It was very deceiving.
太有欺骗性了。

528
00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:52.560
We would have people come visit us on the set, like guests, family members, and they
当时会有客人、家人来片场探班，他们

529
00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:56.400
would go in there thinking that they were real bathrooms, and they weren't.
会以为那是真正的厕所走进去，但其实并不是。

530
00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:56.800
No.
没错。

531
00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:59.500
In the next scene, Dwight calls his sensei.
在下一场戏里，德怀特给他的师傅打了电话。

532
00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:01.800
Jim asks if he's talking to his mother.
吉姆问他是不是在跟他妈妈说话。

533
00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:02.800
I love that.
我太喜欢那段了。

534
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.380
I think John is really good in that scene.
我觉得约翰在那场戏里演得真好。

535
00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:11.660
And then there is his whole talking head about being a sensei, an assistant to the sensei.
然后就是他关于自己是师傅、是师傅助理的那段采访。

536
00:22:11.840 --> 00:22:12.480
What is it?
那是什么意思？

537
00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:17.420
So yeah, Dwight says he's the senpai, which is basically like the assistant to the sensei.
所以，德怀特说他是“前辈”，基本就相当于师傅的助理。

538
00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:17.840
Yeah.
没错。

539
00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:18.580
Although—
虽然——

540
00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:19.520
Not assistant sensei.
不是助理师傅。

541
00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:19.900
Right.
对。

542
00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:21.980
But also, actually, it's not him.
但其实，那个人并不是他。

543
00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:23.380
It's like the girl.
好像是那个女孩。

544
00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:23.820
Remember?
还记得吗？

545
00:22:24.020 --> 00:22:27.520
Because later in the episode, Sensei Ira is like, there's my senpai.
因为在这一集的后面，艾拉师傅说：“那是我的前辈。”

546
00:22:27.560 --> 00:22:29.600
So we learn that it's actually not Dwight.
所以我们才知道原来那个人不是德怀特。

547
00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:30.280
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

548
00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:31.280
I missed that.
我错过了这个细节。

549
00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:31.840
Yeah.
是啊。

550
00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:33.640
The girl that walks through the scene.
就是那个从镜头前走过的女孩。

551
00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:34.020
Yeah.
没错。

552
00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:35.280
Is actually the senpai.
其实是前辈。

553
00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:37.540
Oh, I totally missed that.
哦，我完全没注意到。

554
00:22:37.780 --> 00:22:38.260
All right.
好吧。

555
00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.620
So next, we have Pam's talking head.
接下来是帕姆的访谈片段。

556
00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:47.380
And this is when we find out that today is the day that Michael has to sign time cards,
这一段我们发现，今天就是迈克尔必须签署考勤卡的日子，

557
00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:52.180
purchase order approvals, and expense reports that they're all due at the end of the day.
还有采购订单审批和费用报销单，这些都必须在今天下班前完成。

558
00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:57.080
And this happens a couple times a year, and he always procrastinates wildly on these days.
这种情况一年会发生几次，而他每次都会在这些日子里疯狂拖延。

559
00:22:57.680 --> 00:23:03.120
As a former secretary, I really relate to the dynamic between Pam and Michael in this episode.
作为一名前秘书，我真的对这一集中帕姆和迈克尔之间的互动感同身受。

560
00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:05.900
Because during one of my early secretarial jobs,
因为在我早期的秘书工作中，

561
00:23:06.080 --> 00:23:18.040
I had a boss that would take so long to do his end of the month report that I would have to drive to the airport because the FedEx at the airport had the latest drop time.
我曾遇到过一位老板，他写月度报告总是拖得太久，以至于我不得不开车去机场，因为机场的联邦快递投递截止时间最晚。

562
00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:25.920
I'm saying LAX airport, which anyone who lives in Los Angeles, if I drive to LAX now, it's about a two-hour drive.
我说的是洛杉矶国际机场，任何住在洛杉矶的人都知道，如果我现在开车去那里，大概要花两个小时。

563
00:23:26.140 --> 00:23:30.460
So I would have to drive to the airport for like the 7 p.m.
所以我得开车去机场赶大概晚上7点的，

564
00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.920
It might have even been 9 p.m.
甚至可能是晚上9点的，

565
00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:33.760
FedEx drop.
联邦快递投递。

566
00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:34.920
There's nowhere to park.
那里根本没地方停车。

567
00:23:35.140 --> 00:23:35.900
Nowhere to park.
根本没地方停。

568
00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:37.600
And people are blowing whistles at you.
而且人们还会对你吹哨子。

569
00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:38.000
Yes.
是的。

570
00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:39.320
Like, move out of the way.
就像在催你快走开一样。

571
00:23:39.420 --> 00:23:40.160
It's like chaos.
简直是一团糟。

572
00:23:40.440 --> 00:23:42.640
I do love that Pam calls it the perfect storm.
我很喜欢帕姆把它称为“完美风暴”。

573
00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:43.840
I do too.
我也是。

574
00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:47.000
Also, though, Michael isn't having even to do any work.
不过话说回来，迈克尔甚至都不用做什么工作。

575
00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:48.720
It's not like he's having to put together a report.
他又不是要从头写一份报告。

576
00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:50.540
All he has to do is sign them.
他只需要签个字就行了。

577
00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:51.540
It's so basic.
这太简单了。

578
00:23:51.540 --> 00:23:51.840
That's right.
没错。

579
00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:53.340
It's just his signature.
就只是签个名而已。

580
00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:55.500
It could take him like 20 minutes.
这顶多花他20分钟。

581
00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:55.940
Yeah.
是啊。

582
00:23:56.480 --> 00:23:57.280
And he'd be done.
然后他就搞定了。

583
00:23:57.500 --> 00:24:02.040
This is how, this is why I would get so mad at my boss who couldn't manage to get his report done.
这就是为什么我会对我那位写不出报告的老板那么生气。

584
00:24:02.160 --> 00:24:06.700
Because I would think to myself, it's not new information.
因为我当时心想，这又不是什么新信息。

585
00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:11.280
It's a boilerplate report that you have to do every month.
这只是每个月都要做的例行报告。

586
00:24:11.600 --> 00:24:14.780
It wasn't a special project that sneaked up on us.
又不是什么突然冒出来的特殊项目。

587
00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:15.420
Yeah.
没错。

588
00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:16.660
Time management, dude.
时间管理啊，老兄。

589
00:24:16.820 --> 00:24:20.380
You can see I'm still, I'm still a little angry about it.
你看，我现在提到这事儿还是有点生气。

590
00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:24.440
Well, if I had to drive to the airport to mail something, I'd be ticked off for a long time.
好吧，如果我得开车去机场寄东西，我也会气很久的。

591
00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:24.980
All right.
好了。

592
00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:30.920
So next up, in Michael's attempt to procrastinate, he tells Ryan to update the emergency contacts.
接下来，迈克尔为了拖延时间，让瑞安去更新紧急联系人名单。

593
00:24:31.380 --> 00:24:37.180
So I enter that scene where Michael is telling Ryan to do the emergency contact liSt.
所以我进入了那个迈克尔让瑞安去处理紧急联系人名单的场景。

594
00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:42.980
I was so concentrated on not laughing at Steve, who was being so funny in that scene.
我当时全神贯注地忍着不笑场，因为史蒂夫在那个场景里实在太搞笑了。

595
00:24:43.140 --> 00:24:44.840
It took everything I had.
我使出了浑身解数。

596
00:24:45.020 --> 00:24:52.360
That when BJ would look at me and say the line, updating emergency contacts, I lost it.
当BJ看向我并说出那句台词“更新紧急联系人”时，我彻底破功了。

597
00:24:52.360 --> 00:24:56.700
But I started, it became, you know, in the scenes where you can't stop laughing and you have a trigger?
但我开始……你知道，在那种你无法停止大笑、而且有笑点触发器的情况下吗？

598
00:24:57.100 --> 00:24:57.240
Yeah.
嗯。

599
00:24:57.460 --> 00:25:04.200
It was BJ turning to me and very sadly saying, updating emergency contacts.
就是BJ转过头来，非常悲伤地对我说“更新紧急联系人”。

600
00:25:04.580 --> 00:25:09.940
I think I only got through one scene and I did it by not looking at BJ in the eye.
我想我只拍过一次就过了，而且是因为我没敢直视BJ的眼睛。

601
00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:11.280
Like I stared at his forehead.
就像我盯着他的额头看一样。

602
00:25:11.280 --> 00:25:20.680
I spent nine years looking at Steve Carell's forehead because if I made eye contact with Steve, I used to say he would just like suck out your soul.
我花了九年时间盯着史蒂夫·卡瑞尔的额头看，因为如果我跟史蒂夫有眼神交流，我以前常说他会把你的灵魂吸走。

603
00:25:20.880 --> 00:25:23.320
You made eye contact with him through comedy.
你是通过喜剧跟他进行的眼神交流。

604
00:25:23.620 --> 00:25:26.140
I could not lock eyes with him or I would start laughing.
我不能跟他对视，否则我会笑场。

605
00:25:26.220 --> 00:25:27.000
So I would.
所以我只好。

606
00:25:27.100 --> 00:25:27.940
I would look at his forehead.
我只好盯着他的额头看。

607
00:25:28.620 --> 00:25:29.880
Every conference room scene.
每一场会议室的戏。

608
00:25:29.880 --> 00:25:31.760
I would have to do that or look at someone's ear.
我都得那样做，或者盯着别人的耳朵看。

609
00:25:32.040 --> 00:25:32.480
Yes.
没错。

610
00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:33.520
Or their eyebrows.
或者盯着他们的眉毛。

611
00:25:33.680 --> 00:25:34.480
Yeah, their neck.
对，还有他们的脖子。

612
00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:34.920
Yeah.
是啊。

613
00:25:35.220 --> 00:25:36.520
Just not in the eyes.
就是不能看眼睛。

614
00:25:36.780 --> 00:25:37.960
Not in the eyes.
不能看眼睛。

615
00:25:38.160 --> 00:25:40.580
Well, I thought that was a major Pam Sass moment.
嗯，我觉得那是帕姆非常犀利的一个瞬间。

616
00:25:40.820 --> 00:25:43.660
I think you have two really good Pam Sass moments in this episode.
我觉得这一集里你有两个非常棒的帕姆犀利瞬间。

617
00:25:43.800 --> 00:25:46.100
And one of them is where you just walk out while he's talking.
其中一个就是当他还在说话时，你就直接走开了。

618
00:25:46.380 --> 00:25:48.200
And he's like, ah, she just left it.
然后他就像是，啊，她就这么走了。

619
00:25:48.620 --> 00:25:49.560
When he's finished talking.
等他把话说完。

620
00:25:50.680 --> 00:25:55.100
I was really channeling my real life experience working for that crazy guy.
我当时真的在运用我现实生活中为那个疯子工作的经验。

621
00:25:55.620 --> 00:25:59.060
Michael gets Ryan's phone number in this episode.
迈克尔在这一集里拿到了瑞安的电话号码。

622
00:25:59.060 --> 00:25:59.680
Oh, man.
天哪。

623
00:26:00.080 --> 00:26:00.420
He's so delighted.
他太高兴了。

624
00:26:00.600 --> 00:26:02.040
He keeps calling him and doing voices.
